From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: configure: no prebuilt aarch64 libraries on AArch64 ILP32

configure takes MACHINE from `$CC -dumpmachine` and links
libs/libpfring_mlx_aarch64.a when it exists. That library is LP64, so the
ILP32 link fails. Give ILP32 its own MACHINE so no prebuilt library matches
(the Mellanox module is then not built in, as on other architectures).

---
--- a/userland/configure
+++ b/userland/configure
@@ -3301,6 +3301,10 @@
 
 
 MACHINE=`$CC -dumpmachine | cut -d '-' -f 1`
+# AArch64 ILP32: the prebuilt libs/*_aarch64 libraries are LP64; match none of them
+if echo '__ILP32__' | $CC -E - 2>/dev/null | grep -qx 1; then
+  MACHINE="${MACHINE}_ilp32"
+fi
 CFLAGS=""
 SYS_LIBS=""
 
